* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
* ok = !READJSONROW(c, f)
*
* Reads the next line of the sequential file F that is not blank, parses it as a JSON object or array and puts the data collection in C.
* Gives 1 when it did, 0 at the end of the file (STATUS() 3006, C a null string) or when the line is not JSON (STATUS() 1020, INMAT() the
* place in the line, C a null string).  A JSON Lines file has one value to a line, so a line is never joined to the next.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
function readjsonrow(c, f)
$catalog !readjsonrow

   c = ''
   loop
      readseq line from f else
         return 0
      end
   until trim(line) # '' repeat

   c = jparse(line)
   if status() then
      c = ''
      return 0
   end
   return 1
end

* END-CODE
